bg=cyan</panel_attributes><additional_attributes></additional_attributes></element><element><id>UMLNote</id><coordinates><x>1938</x><y>663</y><w>578</w><h>969</h></coordinates><panel_attributes>Additional constraints and information
--
- The keywords attribute is defined as 
a String that stores a comma-separated list of 
words, where each keyword is followed by a 
comma and a single space 
(e.g., "innovation, technology, research").

- When publishing a project, the kickOffMoment 
must be a valid moment in the future and 
must be prior to or equal to the earliest 
startMoment among all of the project's components. 
Conversely, the closeOutMoment must be a valid 
moment in the future and must be subsequent to or 
equal to the latest endMoment among all 
of the project's components. 

- The effort of a project must be computed in PMs 
(“person-months”) as the sum of active months 
of its components divided by the number of people 
involved.

- When a manager publishes one of their own projects, 
provided it has at least one invention linked to it. 
This implies the publishing of its components. 
However, prior to publishing, all component-level 
validations must be  satisfied; if any validation fails 
for any component,  the publication of the entire
 project will be aborted. 

-  A sponsor must be able to attach any of their 
published sponsorships to any published project. 
An auditor must be able to attach any of their 
published audit reports to any published project. 
The startMoment of any attached sponsorship or 
audit report must be subsequent to the 
closeOutMoment of the project to which it is attached.


bg=red
